    </div>

    <div class="content-text" style="margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        All TX series switches can be configured to function as a <span data-field="comparator_type">{{ comparator_type }}</span>. That is, to detect between two different flow rates or two different temperatures. The switch can monitor for a combination of level and temperature, or flow and temperature with the dual switch point option. With the dual switch point option, the flow rate of a process can be monitored with the millivolt output (approximately 1 volt to 3 millivolts). The millivolt output has an inverse relationship to flow. In this configuration, the unit is two switches contained in one housing.
    </div>

    <div class="content-text" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        The output of basic unit consist of double pole-double throw (DPDT) relay. The dual switch (DS) option includes an other DPDT relay.
    </div>

