  <h2>5.0 INSTALLATION</h2>

  <h3>5.1 Wiring Diagram</h3>
  <p>For mounting threaded units to process line, it is recommended that the process extends into the line being monitored. If a pipe tee is used it is recommended that the leg used to mount the instrument be the same as the instrument connec- tion size (1" MNPT type). The standard instrument (1.8 inch) will fit in a 1 ¼" x 1 ¼" x 1" or larger tee. The 1.2 inch option units are available to insert directly into a 1" or ½" tee.</p>
  <p>For mounting flanged units, the wrench flats on the sensor head should similarly be parallel to flow. For liquid service, fill the process line so that the probe is surrounded by liquid. Then provide wiring to the housing according to the fol- lowing wiring detail.</p>

  <!-- Wiring Diagram Placeholder -->
