  <p>In flow applications the switch must see laminar flow. To assure laminar flow, allow a length of 10 times the diameter of the pipe size after a turn in a pipe before inserting the switch. If inserting the unit in a "tee" the tee size should be the same size as the line or smaller. A larger diameter tee will allow the water to expand and cause false trip to occur because of vortices and/or eddy currents.</p>
